Description: drop the JNI entry points from the symbols file while Java is off
 With the Java bindings switched off (0001), libturbojpeg.so no longer exports
 its 31 Java_org_libjpegturbo_* JNI functions. debian/rules sets
 DPKG_GENSYMBOLS_CHECK_LEVEL=4, which fails on any change, even optional symbols
 disappearing, so remove them from the symbols file, with the TURBOJPEG_1.3
 version node, which holds only JNI functions. Only libturbojpeg-java calls
 them.
Author: Yohane Linux Maintainers <aqours@koiren.ai>
Forwarded: not-needed

